# Files Vercel should not upload.
#
# Vercel uploads the repository, builds it, and serves dist/. It does NOT need
# editor tooling, agent configuration, design references, or the full-resolution
# image masters - and uploading them wastes build time on every deploy.
#
# Nothing listed here is needed to build or serve the site. Removing a line only
# makes the upload larger; it cannot break the build, so this file is safe to
# edit conservatively.

# Agent/editor tooling: 175 files, over half the repository. Not site code.
.opencode/
.claude/
.cursor/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Documentation and planning artefacts. Useful in the repo, dead weight in a
# deployment - and SEO_PERF_PLAN.md and DESIGN.md together are large.
*.md
!README.md
assets-src/
.impeccable/

# Build output. Vercel builds from source, so a committed dist/ would only
# shadow the real build. (It is gitignored already, but an explicit rule means a
# locally-built folder cannot be picked up by a folder-based deploy either.)
dist/
dist-ssr/
.cache/

# Local env. .env.production IS committed on purpose and MUST be uploaded: it
# carries VITE_SITE_URL, which the prerender requires and throws without. Only
# the developer-local variants are excluded.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Measurement artefacts. A committed Lighthouse report is ~1 MB and stale the
# moment the code changes.
lighthouse_report.json
lighthouse-*.json
*.log
